    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0558" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel Marshall S. Carter </hi><anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d281-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to General Marshall </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-17">17 November
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85705. Personal. Reur 1765. The President this morning directed dispatch of the
                    following message to you: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have just seen your 1765 and approve your agreements with General
                            Chou.</p>
                        <pb facs="0559" n="549" xml:id="pg549"/>
                        <p>We want you to know that the circumstances that so far the Chinese have
                            fallen short of acting upon your wise counsels in no way detracts from
                            the high estimate we place upon the quality and utility of what you have
                            done. You have forcefully put before the Chinese a standard of political
                            wisdom and public duty which we feel has profoundly affected their
                            thinking and must in time affect and direct their conduct. Much of an
                            adverse character which might have happened during the past year has not
                            happened thanks to your labours. Constructive results and benefits have
                            come and will come from your mission.</p>
                        <p>You have my constant gratitude and confidence. Signed Harry Truman.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The President leaves this morning for a week at Key West but stated that I could
                    reach him by telephone or the daily courier plane if you desired his urgent
                    action on any matter.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
